error[V0206]: `?` hands the error of this `Result<i32, Error>` back to the caller, but `read_age` returns `Result<i32, string>`, whose error type is `string`
 --> crates/varyk/tests/fixtures/errors/v0206_parse_question_in_result_function/main.vr:2:20
  |
2 |     let age: i32 = text.parse()?;
  |                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `?` hands the error of this `Result<i32, Error>` back to the caller, but `read_age` returns `Result<i32, string>`, whose error type is `string`
  |
  = note: the error types must be the same: an error is never converted into another type
  = note: in Rust terms, `?` returns early with the `Err` or the `None`, so the function's return type must be a `Result` with the same error type, or an `Option`
